      "link": "https://brainly.com/question/29917128",
      "question": "You are debating whether to buy a new computer for $800.00 or a refurbished computer with the same equipment for $640.00. If you are paid $10.00/hour and your deductions are FICA (7.65%), federal tax withholding (12%), and state tax withholding (8%), how many hours do you have to work to pay for the new computer?",
      "answer": "Eighty seven (87)hours, is the time required we have to work to pay for the new** computer**. What does Computer mean? A computer is a data-processing device that can receive, process, store, and output data. It is used for many different tasks, including word processing, data analysis, and gaming. Computers can help with almost any task and are necessary tools in today's world. The word computer comes from the Latin term computare, which means \"to calculate\". Computers process data and produce results by combining hardware and software. If you are paid $10.00/hour and your deductions are FICA (7.65%), Federal Tax Withholding (12%), and State Tax Withholding (8%), then you would have to work 88.3 hours to pay for the new computer. This would be calculated as follows: Total deduction 7.65+12+8 19.65+8 27.65% Now Earnings after deduction 10-10(0.2765) 10-2.765 7.335$ Total hours:- 640/7.335 87.25 87hours To know more about Data analysis, https://brainly.com/question/29376166 #SPJ1",
      "votes": 1
    },
    {
      "link": "https://brainly.com/question/27196392",
      "source": "brainly.co...",
      "question": "You are debating about whether to buy a new computer for $800.00 or a refurbished computer with the same equipment for $640.00. If you are paid $10.00/hour and your deductions are FICA (7.65%), federal tax withholding (12%), and state tax withholding (8%), how many hours do you have to work to pay for the new computer? A. 111 hours B. 98 hours C. 87 hours",
      "answer": "You will have to work 110.5 hours to buy the new computer. What is tax? A tax is some specific financial amount or some other charged taxpayer by the government in order to fund government spending. Given is that you have to buy a new computer for $800.00 or a refurbished computer with the same equipment for $640.00. If you are paid $10.00/hour and your deductions are - FICA (7.65%), Federal tax withholding (12%) State tax withholding (8%). Total money earned after all the deductions - A{n} = 10 - {7.65% of 10 + 12% of 10 + 8% of 10} A{n} = 10 - {7.65/100 x 10 + 12/100 x 10 + 8/100 x 10} A{n} = 10 - {7.65/10 + 12/10 + 8/10} A{n} = 10 - 2.765 • *An **= 7.235 Cost of new computer = $800. For 1 hour. you earned $7.235. Then, you will earn $1 in (1/7.235) hours So, you will earn $800 in (1/7.235 x 800) = 110.5 Therefore, you will have to work 110.5 hours to buy the new computer. To solve more questions on **tax cuts **, visit the link below - https://brainly.com/question/29571101 #SPJ2",
      "votes": 3
    },
    {
      "link": "https://www.coursehero.com/tutors-problems/Math-Other/35577127-You-are-still-debating-about-the-two-different-computers-If-you/",
      "source": "Course Hero",
      "question": "You are still debating about the two different computers. If you are paid $10.00/hour and your deductions are FICA (7.65%), federal tax withholding (12%), and state tax withholding (8%), how many hours do you have to work to pay for the new computer? Be sure to include the following in your response: The answer to the original question The mathematical steps for solving the problem demonstrating mathematical reasoning You are debating about whether to buy a new computer for $800.00 or a refurbished computer with the same equipment for $640.00. If a savings account earns 4.5% APR interest, how much do you really save with a refurbished computer if you put the difference into the savings account for a year? Be sure to include the following in your response: • The answer to the original question The mathematical steps for solving the problem demonstrating mathematical reasoning",
      "answer": "ANSWER : 1. ) Hours needed to work for the purchase of a new computer :COMPUTER 1 ($800) = 110.57 hoursCOMPUTER 2 ($640) = 88.46 hours2. Total savings after 1 year interest to the difference of the two computers :Total Savings = $167.2 Here is the solution and explanation of the problem :1. ) For the first question on \"How many hours needed to work for the purchase of a new computer?\"a. ) Let us first deduct the taxes from the rate per hour to get the NET SALARY RATE PER HOUR :Salary per hour : $10Deductions : 7.65% (FICA) , 12% (Federal Tax Withholding) , 8% (State Tax Withholding)NET SALARY = $10 - ((0.0765 + 0.12 + 0.08) x (10))NET SALARY = $7.235b. ) Next is to compute for the NUMBER OF HOURS for the two computers so that we may compare and get the difference :* For the COMPUTER 1 (New Computer) , cost is $800 NUMBER OF HOURS = $800 / $7.235NUMBER OF HOURS = 110.57 hours* For the COMPUTER 2 (Refurbished Computer) , cost is $640NUMBER OF HOURS = $640 / $7.235NUMBER OF HOURS = 88.46 …",
